  clock: 3  # 680a
  nonce: 680a  # 680a
  message: "Fixed in PR #1577 (merge 4d5a8ec889), folded into scheme v9. Root cause: perl._get_current_package read a block-form package_statement (package B { }) as a statement-form one, so a sub inside it took the package before it (A::go) and a sub after the block kept the block's package. Fix: an enclosing block-form package names its subs; a statement-form package in an enclosing scope applies otherwise; block-form siblings are skipped. Evidence: f3/live/sweep2.py (this item's filed repro) on 4d5a8ec889 -> perl survivors 2, same 2, moved 0, unmatched 0 (was unmatched B::go); gate fixture perl-blocks (package A { sub go } / package B { sub go } / sub top) 3/3 same via hypergumbo run; unit test test_perl_block_packages_name_their_own_subs pins A::go, B::go, top, C::h. Statement-form unchanged: 0 perl ids changed on the code corpus sample."  # 680a
